# Application configuration: read by internal/config/config.go and delivered to
# the container through compose.yaml's `environment:`. A commented line is a
# default the application already uses — uncomment one only to change it.
# scripts/check-env-example.sh fails the build when a variable either this
# application or compose.yaml can be configured with is missing from here.
SCHALL_HTTP_ADDRESS=:8080
SCHALL_DATABASE_URL=postgres://schall:schall@localhost:5432/schall?sslmode=disable
SCHALL_LOG_LEVEL=info
# How long startup waits for a database that is still accepting no connections.
SCHALL_DATABASE_STARTUP_TIMEOUT=60s
SCHALL_MUSICBRAINZ_USER_AGENT=Schall/0.1.0 (https://github.com/pxldi/schall)
# The MusicBrainz web service Schall asks about releases and recordings. Point
# it at a mirror; unset, the public instance is used.
# SCHALL_MUSICBRAINZ_BASE_URL=https://musicbrainz.org/ws/2
SCHALL_LIBRARY_ALLOWED_ROOTS=/music

# The managed library: where both acquisition routes write what they take in. On
# its own it turns nothing on — startup refuses it unless one of the two paths
# below is set as well — and without it neither route can be turned on at all.
# SCHALL_IMPORT_LIBRARY_PATH=/music
# Where the download client leaves completed downloads. Unset, the download
# import route is off and nothing is taken in from finished transfers.
# SCHALL_DOWNLOAD_INBOX_PATH=/downloads
# Where a browser upload waits to be validated. Unset, browser uploads are off.
# It must be outside every music folder, or a scan would index a half-written
# upload as music the library holds; startup checks this rather than trusting it.
# SCHALL_UPLOAD_STAGING_PATH=/uploads

# The Chromaprint binary that turns audio into a fingerprint. Unset, fpcalc is
# looked for on PATH; not finding it costs acoustic identification, and a copy
# only the audio could admit is held or sent to review instead of imported.
# SCHALL_FPCALC_PATH=fpcalc
# The yt-dlp binary used for YouTube searches and audio excerpts. Unset, YouTube
# acquisition is disabled.
# SCHALL_YTDLP_PATH=/usr/local/bin/yt-dlp
# The transcoder that makes a copy playable in a browser, so a review item can
# be listened to before it is decided about. Unset, ffmpeg is looked for on
# PATH; not finding it costs the preview and nothing else.
# SCHALL_FFMPEG_PATH=ffmpeg
# Where those transcodes are kept between requests. Scratch by nature — deleting
# it costs a re-encode. Unset, a schall-previews folder under the system
# temporary directory is used, which a container restart empties.
# SCHALL_PREVIEW_CACHE_PATH=/tmp/schall-previews

# How the library's path in Schall differs from the same library's path in
# Navidrome, as comma-separated local=remote pairs. Unset is the identity
# mapping, which is right wherever both read the library through the same path;
# where the two mounts disagree, playlist sync pairs nothing at all without this.
# SCHALL_NAVIDROME_PATH_MAP=/music=/music-schall

# Authentication. `open` (the default) serves every request and logs one
# warning at startup. `proxy` serves an /api/ request only when the reverse
# proxy vouched for the X-authentik-* identity headers with the key below, or
# when the request carries an app token minted in Settings → Phone. Any other
# value is refused at startup. Development, the browser tests and the seed
# run open.
# SCHALL_AUTH=open

# The value the reverse proxy puts in X-Schall-Proxy-Key. Schall reads the
# identity headers only when this matches. Required in proxy mode unless
# SCHALL_AUTH_TRUSTED_PROXIES is set.
# SCHALL_AUTH_PROXY_KEY=

# Comma-separated CIDR blocks, checked against the TCP peer address, whose
# identity headers are believed without the key. Weaker: every host on a
# listed network is then a trusted proxy.
# SCHALL_AUTH_TRUSTED_PROXIES=10.42.0.0/16

# Compose host settings: never read by the application. These are the ${...}
# interpolations in compose.yaml that set the container user and the host folders
# it binds.

# The host interface the API is published on. Schall has no authentication, so
# anyone who can reach this address can change settings, upload, delete and drive
# every job. Loopback keeps that to this machine; 0.0.0.0 serves the whole
# network and should only be set with something in front that asks who is
# calling. This is the host publish only — the container listens on
# SCHALL_HTTP_ADDRESS inside its own network namespace either way.
SCHALL_BIND_ADDRESS=127.0.0.1
SCHALL_MUSIC_PATH=./music
# Host folder where slskd places completed downloads. Schall reads but never
# changes this folder.
SCHALL_DOWNLOADS_PATH=./downloads
# Mount mode for that folder. Keep it read-only unless you intend to set the
# import retention policy to remove imported files, which needs to write there.
SCHALL_DOWNLOADS_MODE=ro
# Host folder behind the staging area the container sees at
# SCHALL_UPLOAD_STAGING_PATH — the two are a pair, one naming the host side and
# one the container side. Scratch space: what is in it is either on its way into
# the library or a refusal nobody has discarded yet.
SCHALL_UPLOADS_PATH=./uploads
SCHALL_UID=1000
SCHALL_GID=1000
